When something is nerfed, it is a change to the original intent of the card to make it weaker. This is explaining the original intent of the card, not altering that intent in the least.

[quote="Powerhound_2000"]

Then how that work with a charge then? &nbsp;Shouldn&#39;t that deal 2 damage to each non hero target. &nbsp;It&#39;s not using the strike so it should not be dealing a base of one melee damage.

[/quote]

Really? Fine if we really have to do this.

If Fixer has Jack Handle in play, and plays charge, read charge as &quot;deal all non-hero targets 2 melee damage.&quot;

If Fixer has obtained the Rod of Anubis and uses it&#39;s power while wielding Jack handle, read it as &quot;deal all non-hero targets 2 infernal damage.&quot;

If Fixer is facing Plague Rat and is Fixer is&nbsp;infected with Jack Handle, read the infection as &quot;deal all non-hero targets 1 toxic damage.&quot;

If&nbsp;Fixer is facing Plague Rat and is Fixer is&nbsp;infected with Jack Handle and Afflicted Frenzy is in play, read the Afflicted Frenzy as &quot;deal all non-hero targets X melee damage.&quot;

If Fixer is facing The Ennead and Osiris is in play, when an Ankh card enters the trash while Fixer has Jack Handle, read Osiris&#39; card as &quot;deal each non-hero target 1 infernal damage.&quot;

If Fixer is facing Iron Legacy a Demoralizing Presence is in play, then read it as &quot;deal all non-hero targets 1 psychic damage.&quot;

Do I need to continue, or have you gotten the point?
